[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom (anticipated): an Apple-Silicon Mac still on an older macOS
version would pass the arch gate (bdce01c) but could still silently run
into a cask-install failure later, at Step 3.

Root cause: Whisky's own cask metadata requires both `arch: arm64` and
`macos >= 14` — only the architecture half had been gated so far.

Fix: added a matching soft version-gate check to Pre-flight, same gentle
tone as the arch-gate message.
